---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Providers &amp; CLI contract — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px">remainder</div>
    <h1>Providers &amp; CLI contract</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Provider selection, output formats, flags, --all, and exit codes. An
      explicit selection first checks a short-lived, account/source-bound
      observation cache, then reads the local credential file and makes a
      bounded request on a miss.
    </p>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2 style="margin:0 0 14px">Providers</h2>
      <div class="kv md" style="grid-template-columns:110px 1fr">
        <div class="k">codex</div>
        <div class="v">
          Reads <code>$CODEX_HOME/auth.json</code> or <code
            >~/.codex/auth.json</code
          > and makes a bounded request to the Codex usage endpoint on a miss.
          The default profile is the single CODEX_HOME context selected by the
          process environment.
        </div>
        <div class="k">claude</div>
        <div class="v">
          The single selected <code>$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.credentials.json</code>
          or <code>~/.claude/.credentials.json</code> context. Verifies the
          account through the profile endpoint before reading quota; preserves
          session, weekly, model, and separate paid usage windows. No Keychain
          or refresh fallback.
        </div>
        <div class="k">grok</div>
        <div class="v">
          The selected Grok consumer file context. Shared and product
          percentages remain separate from prepaid credits, and account identity
          stays unknown.
        </div>
        <div class="k">cursor</div>
        <div class="v">
          The selected CLI auth file on Linux. Included percentages and spend
          amounts in cents remain separate. On macOS, a new observation requires
          <code>--allow-keychain-prompt</code>; editor SQLite remains
          unsupported.
        </div>
        <div class="k">devin</div>
        <div class="v">
          The Devin CLI credential file (<code>DEVIN_CREDENTIALS</code>, then
          <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/devin/credentials.toml</code>, then <code
            >~/.local/share/devin/credentials.toml</code
          >). One bounded Connect JSON GetUserStatus call; normalizes daily and
          weekly quota percentages, resets, and reported ACU or credit balances.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Formats</h2>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>remainder --provider codex --profile default                   <span class="c"># deterministic one-line compact output</span></div>
        <div>remainder --provider codex --profile default --format json     <span class="c"># versioned JSON observation</span></div>
        <div>remainder --provider codex --profile default --format toon     <span class="c"># the same facts as a TOON document</span></div>
        <div>remainder value --provider PROVIDER --profile PROFILE --window WINDOW --field remaining</div>
        <div>remainder --all                                                <span class="c"># Codex, Claude, Grok, Devin concurrently, then Cursor on Linux and macOS</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        The scalar fields also include <code>reset</code>, <code>duration</code
        >, and <code>pace</code>. --all cannot be combined with provider,
        profile, or account flags and does not discover profiles. Mixed JSON
        contains separate observations and provider-scoped failures; compact
        output remains one line. A provider failure preserves other usable
        observations with exit 3; no usable observations produces exit 1 and
        empty stdout.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2 style="margin:0 0 14px">Exit codes</h2>
      <div class="kv" style="grid-template-columns:60px 1fr">
        <div class="k">0</div>
        <div class="v">
          The selected evidence is usable, including zero, exhausted, and
          unlimited values.
        </div>
        <div class="k">1</div>
        <div class="v">The observation is unavailable.</div>
        <div class="k">2</div>
        <div class="v">
          Invocation or selection is invalid. Selecting an unknown or
          non-applicable pace exits 2 with an explicit undefined-value error.
        </div>
        <div class="k">3</div>
        <div class="v">A partial observation was rendered.</div>
        <div class="k">130</div>
        <div class="v">
          Interruption. SIGINT is handled through a context-owned interrupt
          path.
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:14px 0 0">
        <code>--help</code> and <code>--version</code> write to stdout and exit
        successfully. An invocation without a provider selection or --all writes
        an honest unavailable message to stderr and exits nonzero. Unknown flags
        and positional commands write an actionable error to stderr and exit
        nonzero.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
